<title>BRAZIL: Brazil moves to regulate ADR issues by locals.</title>
<headline>Brazil moves to regulate ADR issues by locals.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) authorized the publication of norms governing the issue of American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) by local banks, a CMN document said.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, President Fernando Henrique Cardoso signed a decree allowing Brazilian banks to issue abroad ADRs convertible to non-voting shares.</p>
<p>Banks will not be able to trade voting, or ordinary, shares abroad.</p>
<p>The move is aimed at drawing foreign capital to local banks at a time when many are investing in technology to meet growing competition.</p>
</text>
